<title>USA: M.W. Kellogg Co process on-stream at INCITEC.</title>
<headline>M.W. Kellogg Co process on-stream at INCITEC.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>M.W. Kellogg Co, a subsidiary of Dresser Industries Inc, said Monday that its advanced ammonia process unit has been brought on stream at the Gibson Island ammonia plant in Brisbane, Australia, owned by a subsidiary of ICI Australia Ltd, INCITEC Ltd.</p>
<p>Kellogg said that the process has increased ammonia production capacity at the plant by 11 percent, to 800 metric tons a day, while substantially reducing energy consumption.</p>
<p>Kellogg said the unit passed its test run on initial start-up and was accepted by INCITEC after the performance test exceeded expectations.</p>
</text>
